$DATUM Synthesis of 4-substituted benzaldehyde (3a-i) A mixture of substituted
phenol 1a-i (37.4 mmol), 4-ﬂuorobenzaldehyde 2 (37.4 mmol), and potassium
car-bonate (38.8 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (30 ml) was reﬂuxed for
16-18 h under nitrogen. After cooling, the product was extracted from the
reaction mixture and puriﬁed by chromatography. (3e). 4-(4-bromophenoxy)
benzaldehyde (3e) Yield: 72%. m.p.: 47 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1 ) ν: 1662 (C=O),
1241 (-O-); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 9.81 (s, 1H, -CHO), 6.80-7.82 (a
set of signals, 8H, Ar-H); MS (m/z, %): 276.95 (M+ + 1 for 79Br, 100.00),
278.93 (M+ + 1 for 81Br, 96.70).
