$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: SNAr. General Procedure A. As an example,
potassium carbonate (2 equiv, 400 mmol) was added to a solution of
4-hydroxybenzaldehyde (1 equiv), 4-halobenzonitrile (1 equiv, 200 mmoL),
and dimethylaceta-mide (0.4M, 475 mL). The reaction was heated to 100 °C
for 2 h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature and then poured into
1.4 L of ice water. The resulting tan solid was collected by filtration,
washed with water (2 x 150 mL), and then dried in a vacuum oven. The
4-(4-formylphenoxy)benzonitrile. 3-Fluoro-4-(4-formylphenoxy)benzonitrile
(21). Compound 21 was prepared from 4-hydroxybenzaldehyde and 3,
4-difluoro-benzonitrile using general procedure A. Yield (72%). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, DMSO): 9.92 (s, 1H), 7.98-7.89 (m, 2H), 7.76 (dd, J = 1.8, 10.3
Hz, 1H), 7.65-7.56 (m, 1H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.22-7.12 (m, 2H).
