$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Reaction Conditions for the synthesis of diazadioxacalix[4]arenes
5: Under ambient atmosphere, an air-dried flask was charged with
nucleophile 2 (0.50 mmol, 1 equiv) and electrophile 1 (204 mg, 1.0 mmol,
2 equiv). DMF (2.0 mL) was added, followed by (iPr)2NEt (0.400 mL, 2.4
mmol, 4.7 equiv for 2b-2d; 0.600 mL, 3.5 mmol, 7.0 equiv for 2a used as
its bis-hydrochloride salt), and the reaction was stirred for 2 h at 25
°C. Diphenol 4 (0.50 mmol, 1 equiv) was then added, and the reaction was
heated to 60 °C and allowed to stir for an additional 2 h. The reaction
was cooled to room temperature, and then the product precipitated by the
addition of 0.5 M HCl (10.0 mL). Unpurified 5 was then isolated by vacuum
filtration, washed with water (10.0 mL) and dried in vacuo. The product
was then purified by flash chromatography as described below.
10-methoxy-23-carbomethoxy-4,6,16,18-tetranitro-8,14-diaza-2,20-dioxacalix[4]arene
(5a): 1, 2a, and 4a were condensed under the General Reaction Conditions
for the synthesis of diazadioxacalix[4]arenes 5, and the product purified
via flash column chromatography through silica (gradient 0-4% CH3CN in
CH2Cl2) to yield 230 mg 5a as a red-orange solid (72%). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 9.69 (s, 1H), 9.53 (s, 1H), 9.13 (s, 1H), 9.13 (s, 1H), 7.75
(t, 1H, J = 1.9 Hz), 7.69 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 7.21 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz),
7.14-7.11 (m, 2H), 7.07-7.04 (m, 1H), 3.94 (s, 3H), 3.89 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.4, 157.7, 157.5, 154.1, 153.7, 153.5, 147.9,
146.9, 135.2, 129.4, 129.4, 129.1, 128.0, 127.2, 127.0, 126.7, 126.2,
124.2, 121.2, 119.3, 113.7, 100.5, 56.2, 53.0; IR (ATR): 3325, 3090,
2922, 1727, 1623, 1575, 1506, 1435, 1330, 1294, 1261, 1232, 1123, 1057,
997, 832, 743 cm-1; HRMS [MALDI(-) with a DHB matrix] calculated for
(M-H)- [C27H18N6O13]-: 633.08591, found: 633.08782.
