$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4-Bromo-phenoxy)-benzoic acid ethyl ester. Following a modified
procedure by I. K. Kostakis,[3] a mixture of 2-ethyliodobenzoate (2.76 g,
10 mmol, 1.0 eq.), 4-bromophenol (3.46 g, 20 mmol, 2.0 eq.), K2CO3 (1.52
g, 11 mmol, 1.1 eq.), Cu powder (318 mg, 5 mmol, 0.5 eq.) and KI (830 mg,
5 mmol, 0.5 eq.) in 120 mL DMF were stirred at 110 °C for 24 h.
Monitoring the reaction progress by GC/MS, another 318 mg Cu powder (5
mmol, 0.5 eq.) were added to get full consumption of 2-ethyliodobenzoate
and the mixture was stirred at 110 °C for another 24 h. The reaction was
quenched through the addition of H2O and the mixture was extracted with
EtOAc three times. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The remaining
4-bromophenol could be removed by Kugelrohr distillation (120 °C, 5 x
10-1 bar, 2 h) to give the crude product, which was further purified by
flash chromatography (3 x 15 cm silica, pentane/EtOAc = 40/1 → 20/1). The
desired product could be obtained in 72% (2.32 g, 7.21 mmol) yield as
light yellow oil. 2-(4-Bromo-phenoxy)-benzoic acid ethyl ester, 72% (2.32
g, 7.21 mmol) yield RF (pentane/EtOAc = 50/1): 0.21; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): 1.22 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H, CH3), 4.25 (q, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H, CH2),
6.78-6.82 (m, 2H, Har), 7.01 (dd, J = 8.2 Hz, 0.9 Hz, 1H, Har), 7.24 (dt,
J = 7.6 Hz, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H, Har), 7.38-7.42 (m, 2H, Har), 7.50 (ddd, J =
8.2 Hz, J = 7.5 Hz, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H, Har), 7.93 (dd, J = 7.8 Hz, J = 1.8
Hz, 1H, Har); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 14.2 (CH3), 61.3 (CH2), 115.2
(Car), 119.2 (Car), 121.8 (Car), 124.2 (Car), 124.5 (Car), 132.1 (Car),
132.7 (Car), 133.8 (Car), 155.2 (Cq), 157.4 (Cq), 165.6 (CO); ESI-MS:
calculated [C15H13BrO3H]+: 321.1021, found: 321.1027; calculated
[C15H13BrO3Na]+: 342.9940, found: 342.9946; calculated
[[C15H13BrO3)2Na]+: 664.9970, found: 664.9976; GC/MS, Rt: 9.4 min, (EI)
m/z (%): 322.0 (36), 320.0 (36), 277.0 (14), 275.0 (15), 197.0 (10),
196.1 (34), 168.1 (24), 139.1 (24), 121.0 (100), 120.0 (10); ATR-FTIR
(cm-1): 1716, 1478, 1449, 1292, 1230, 1126, 1078, 1069, 1007, 824, 754,
708.
