$DATUM 1310-58-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.2.1 Synthesis of halogenated nitro catechol diphenyl ether 1a-1f 0.0110
mol halogenated hydroxydiphenyl ether was heated to fusion followed by
the addition of 0.0105 mol KOH. The reaction was conducted for 15 min.
0.0100 mol substituted nitro chlorobenzene was added in portions, and the
mixture was heated to 150-175 °C. The reaction process was detected by
TLC (developing agent : petroleum ether : toluene = 1 : 1, V : V). After
the reaction was complete, the reaction system was cooled and washed with
80 °C 5 % NaOH solution (3 × 15 mL) and boiling water three times. The
hot mixture was poured into cold water. The solution was cooled, filtered
and dried to afford the crude product as a yellow granule, which was
further recrystallized from anhydrous ethanol to give product 1a-1f as a
yellowish crystal. 1a, 71.5 %, yellowish crystal m.p. 76-78 ℃; 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 6.84 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.91 (d, J = 7.2 Hz,
1H, ArH), 7.03 (dd, J = 7.2, 2.2 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.13 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H,
ArH), 7.15-7.13 (m, 1H, ArH), 7.21-7.19 (m, 1H, ArH), 7.25 (dd, J = 8.0,
2.6 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.36 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.54-7.50 (m, 1H, ArH),
7.95-7.93 (m, 1H, ArH); IR (KBr) ν: 3086 (Ar), 2382 (ArOAr), 1184 (ArH),
1100 (ArCl) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 409 (M+, 100), 289 (35), 254 (99), 232
(40). Anal. cacld for C18H10Cl3NO4: C 52.65, H 2.45, N 3.41; found C
52.63, H 2.45, N 3.40.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
