$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2,3,5,6-Tetrafluoro-4-(4-iodophenoxy)benzaldehyde (14). 4-Iodophenol (3;
2.2 g, 10 mmol) and pentafluorobenzaldehyde (1; 1.23 mL, 10 mmol) were
dissolved in DMF (10 mL) and KF (1.162 g, 20 mmol) was added. After 1 h,
H2O (50 mL) was added and the resulting suspension was extracted with
EtOAc (3 × 40 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated. The solid was crystallized (cyclohexane) to obtain pure
aldehyde 14. 1,3-Bis(2,3,5,6-tetrafluoro-4-formylphenoxy)benzene (23),
yield 72%. Mp 147-148 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.75-6.82 (m, 3 H,
ArH), 7.34 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1 H, ArH), 10.31 (br s, 2 H, CHO). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 105.5, 111.7, 111.7, 131.0, 138.4, 141.2, 147.5,
157.5, 181.7. HRMS (EI): m/z [M+] calcd for C20H6F8O4: 462.0138; found:
462.0155. Anal. Calcd for C20H6F8O4: C, 51.97; H, 1.31. Found: C, 51.93;
H, 1.21.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Straightforward transformation of pentafluorobenzaldehyde into
4-aryloxy-2,3,5,6-tetrafluorobenzaldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
