$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-(p-methoxy)phenoxy-6-methoxybenzaldehyde 7e. A mixture of
2-fluoro-6-methoxybenzaldehyde (1.00 g, 6.49 mmol), p-methoxyphenol (805
mg, 6.49 mmol) and K2CO3 (986 mg, 7.14 mmol) in DMF (7.0 mL) was refluxed
for 4 h. The mixture was cooled to room temperature and diluted with
CHCl3 and quenched by the addition of water. The organic layer was washed
with water, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude material was purified by distillation (220 ºC, 1 Torr) and
recrystallized in hexane/EtOAc. The corresponding aldehyde 7e (1.19 g,
4.61 mmol, 71%) as colorless plates. M.p. 78.3-79.3ºC; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, 298 K): TM 10.59 (s, 1H, -CHO), 7.35 (dd, J 1 = 8.5, J 2 = 8.5 Hz,
1H, Ar-H), 7.03-6.97 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 6.93-6.85 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 6.64 (d, J=
8.5 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 6.35 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 3.93 (s, 3H, -OCH 3),
3.81 (s, 3H, -OCH 3) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K): TM 189.1 (1C,
-CHO), 161.8, 161.6, 156.6, 149.3, 135.6, 121.4, 115.9, 115.0, 109.3,
105.4 (12C, Ar-C), 56.3 (1C, -OCH3), 55.8 (1C, -OCH3) ppm; IR (KBr); 1682
({CHO), 1241 ({Ar-OAr) cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C15H14O4: C, 69.76; H, 5.46;
O, 24.78. Found: C, 69.16; H, 5.32.
