$DATUM 22-hexyl-26-methyl-4,6,16,18-tetranitro-8,14-diaza-2,20-dioxacalix[4]arene
(5g): Under ambient atmosphere, a flask was charged with 2e (61 mg, 0.50
mmol, 1 equiv) and 1 (204 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2 equiv). DMF (2.0 mL) was added,
followed by (iPr)2NEt (0.400 mL, 2.4 mmol, 3.5 equiv), and the reaction
was heated to 40 °C and stirred for 2 h. Diphenol 4c (97 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1
equiv) was then added, and the reaction was heated to 70 °C and allowed
to stir for an additional 2 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, and then the product precipitated by the addition of 0.5 M
HCl (10.0 mL). Unpurified 5 was then isolated by vacuum filtration,
washed with water (10.0 mL) and dried in vacuo. The product was purified
via flash column chromatography through silica (gradient 0-2% CH3CN in
CH2Cl2) to yield 230 mg 5g as a bright yellow solid (71%). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.70 (s, 1H), 9.69 (s, 1H), 9.21 (s, 2H), 9.19 (s, 1H),
7.38 (t, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.32 (d, 1H, J = 8.3 Hz), 7.24 (d, 1H, J = 7.4
Hz), 7.19 (d, 1H, J = 7.9 Hz), 6.93 (dd, 1H, J = 8.3, 2.4 Hz), 6.80 (d,
1H, J = 2.5 Hz), 5.37 (s, 1H), 5.36 (s, 1H), 2.41 (t, 2H, J = 7.7 Hz),
1.93 (s, 3H), 1.54-1.41 (m, 2H), 1.27-1.21 (m, 6H), 0.88 (t, 1H, J = 7.1
Hz); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.8, 158.1, 151.1, 151.0, 147.6, 147.5,
136.7, 136.7, 135.2, 134.5, 133.2, 129.3, 129.2, 129.1, 129.1, 128.9,
128.2, 128.1, 125.7, 125.6, 120.5, 115.4, 99.3, 98.6, 31.4, 29.8, 29.2,
28.7, 22.4, 14.0, 12.8; IR (ATR): 3332, 3091, 2927, 1623, 1571, 1506,
1416, 1357, 1330, 1295, 1270, 1235, 1059, 831, 795, 742, 691 cm-1; HRMS
[MALDI(-) with a DHB matrix] calculated for (M-H)- [C31H28N6O10]-:
643.17941, found: 643.18038.
