$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the linear trimer: To a solution of
1,5-difluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene (1.68gr, 8.24 mmol) and resorcinol
derivative (2.75 mmol) in acetone (25 ml) was added K2CO3 (1.51gr, 11.0
mmol). The solution was stirred at r.t. for 6 hrs, then potassium
carbonate was filtered out. After most of the solvent was removed under
reduced pressure, the residue was dissolved in CHCl3, and then washed
with saturated solution of NH4Cl, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (hexane:EA
7:3). The product as pale yellow solid in 70-80% yield. 70% yield. 1H NMR
(400MHz, DMSO-d6): δ, ppm 8.91 (d, 2H, JHF=7.7 Hz, ArH), 7.66 (t, 1H,
J=8.5Hz, ArH), 7.53 (td, 2H, JHF=12.3Hz, 3.8Hz, 3.3Hz, ArH), 7.33 (t, 1H,
J=2.3Hz, ArH), 7.27 (dd, 2H, J=8.2Hz, 2.3Hz, ArH). 13C NMR (400MHz,
DMSO-d6): δ, ppm 159.62, 156.93, 155.82 (d, JCF=11.5Hz), 155.23, 135.85,
132.83, 125.25, 118.34, 112.82, 109.43 (d, JCF=27.6Hz).
