$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 7 A mixture of the corresponding
benzofuran intermediate (1.0 equiv), the corresponding catechol (2.5
equiv), Cs2CO3 (2.2 equiv), CuI (0.2 equiv), N,N-dimethyl glycine
hydrochloride (0.4 equiv) in dioxane (5.0 mL per mmol benzofuran
intermediate) in a sealed tube was heated to 90 ºC under N2 atmosphere
for 18 h. The cooled mixture was partitioned between ethyl acetate and
water. The organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was
extracted with ethyl acetate. The combined organic layers were washed
with brine, dried over Na2SO4, concentrated by rotary evaporation, and
purified by column chromatography. 47a-e and 47g-h.
4-(2-methoxyphenoxy)-6-methylbenzofuran-2-carbonitrile (47b) (71%). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.31 (s, 1H), 7.23 (d, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H), 7.05 -
7.01 (m, 1H), 6.75 (dd, J = 8.1, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 6.66 (s, 1H) 6.64 - 6.59
(m, 2H), 3.69 (s, 3H), 2.39 (s, 3H). LC-MS (ES) for C17H13NO3 [M+1]+
280.07.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
