N-(4-(4-chlorophenoxy)phenyl)benzamide (Table 2, entry 17). Purified by
column chromatography on silica gel using acetone/petroleum ether (1:6)
as eluent to obtain the title compound as a white solid. Yield 70%, m.p.
172-173°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 7.87 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.84
(brs, 1H), 7.61 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 7.55 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (t, J
= 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.01 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.93
(d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 165.70, 156.24, 153.37,
134.83, 133.77, 131.92, 129.72, 128.84, 128.15, 127.00, 122.08, 119.73,
119.67. IR (cm-1) 3267, 1648, 1607, 1508, 1486, 1404, 1255, 1194, 1162,
1092, 1010, 877, 827, 815, 716, 695. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C19H14ClNO2
([M+Na]+) 346.0605, found 346.0604.
