$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Preparation of Diphenylether (13-28).
Method C (microwave): A mixture of N-aryl-5-chloro-2-nitroaniline (1
equiv) and 2,6-dimethylphenol (1.2 equiv) in DMF (3 mL) in the presence
of anhydrous potassium carbonate (2 equiv) was irradiated under microwave
with stirring at 190 °C for 15 min. The mixture was poured into
ice-water, pH adjusted to neutral with 5% HCl aq, and the mixture
extracted with EtOAc three times. After removal of organic solvent in
vacuo, crude product was purified by PTLC or a silica column (eluent:
petroleum ether/EtOAc).
N-(4'-Cyanophenyl)-2,4-dinitro-5-(2'',4'',6''-trimethylphenoxy)-aniline
(22). Method C, yield 70%, starting with 637 mg (2 mmol) of 11 and 286 mg
(2.1 mmol) of 2,4,6-trimethylphenol to afford 580 mg of 22, yellow solid,
mp 223-225 °C. 1H NMR δ ppm 2.00 (6H, s, 2 x CH3), 2.22 (3H, s, CH3),
5.92 (1H, s, ArH-6), 6.95 (2H, s, ArH-3'', 5''), 7.27 (2H, d, J = 8.8 Hz,
ArH-2', 6'), 7.72 (2H, d, J = 8.8 Hz, ArH-3', 5'), 8.95 (1H, s, ArH-3),
10.04 (1H, s, NH). MS m/z (%): 419 (M + 1, 100). HPLC purity: 98.3%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (in stage 1), thermal (in stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diarylaniline Derivatives as a Distinct Class of HIV-1 Non-nucleoside
Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors
